    "body": "Adds the option `verbose` which (when set to `false`) disables messages like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"ib\" found covering region within 50 lines and `search_method = 'next'`.\r\n```\r\n\r\nNeovim doesn't print any message if you try to access built-in text-objects like `i\"`, `a)`, that don't exist. Therefore I think it's reasonable to have an option to disable mini.ai's messages.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-02-24T16:48:26Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for PR! \r\n\r\n> Neovim doesn't print any message if you try to access built-in text-objects like `i\"`, `a)`, that don't exist. Therefore I think it's reasonable to have an option to disable mini.ai's messages.\r\n\r\nThe reason is explained in [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/135#issuecomment-1263305433) of the issue for this specific functionality.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nAdding `verbose` option is tracked in #146. I plan to use it a little bit more broader than suppressing these \"not found messages\".\r\n\r\nIt will be a part of work scope for after the release.",
