        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski  Ok, I see!\r\n\r\nBtw, I noticed that you use `echo` to print the messages. Is there any reason why you're not using `vim.notify` which allow users to use plugins like [nvim-notify](https://github.com/rcarriga/nvim-notify) to display the messages in a floating popup window instead of at the bottom? That way you're not forced to \"press any button\" when the message is multiple lines long.",
