        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Btw, I noticed that you use `echo` to print the messages. Is there any reason why you're not using `vim.notify` which allow users to use plugins like [nvim-notify](https://github.com/rcarriga/nvim-notify) to display the messages in a floating popup window instead of at the bottom?\r\n\r\nWell, that is exactly the reason. There are many messages that I find helpful (especially for new users), but which are issued quite frequently. Like \"Enter character\" reminder after one second of not pressing anything, etc. Initially it did use `vim.notify`, but stopped in 1764bcfb.\r\n\r\n> That way you're not forced to \"press any button\" when the message is multiple lines long.\r\n\r\nYou shouldn't have the need to \"press any button\" when this type of message is long. It was handled in b8e9fccd. If you experience any hit-enter-prompt during any type of \"information messages\" (i.e. not errors or warning-like messages dedicated to grab user's attention).",
