        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've decided to go the route of global/buffer-local variables for this one, as it more cleanly indicates that this approach is universal for all modules.\r\n\r\nIn latest `main` branch you should be able to set `vim.g.miniai_silence = true` in your Lua config file and no messages should be shown (neither helper message after one idle second, nor \"No textobject ... found\"). Sorry, not exactly what you were suggesting here, but this is the way now.\r\n\r\nThanks for the final push to make me implement this.",
